  "answer": "ANSWER: The powered descent section is Section 5.3 of the Apollo 11 Mission Report, and it runs from page 5-4 to page 5-6. The redesignation happened because the approach path led into a large crater, which forced an unplanned change of landing point (src: Apollo 11 Mission Report p.5-4). The crew took manual control at about 600 feet and landed about 1100 feet downrange of the first aim point (src: Apollo 11 Mission Report p.5-5).\nFILES: index.md, sources/apollo-11-mission-report/apollo-11-mission-report-ch-05.md",
